        "type": "text",
        "text": "{\"recorded_count\": 23, \"total_count\": 23, \"missing_ids\": [], \"complete\": true, \"results\": [{\"item_id\": \"FT-1\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No way to attach the seller's own photos; only canned stock images can be added\", \"actual\": \"The create-listing form has no file input at all (document.querySelectorAll('input[type=file]').length === 0). The \\\"Add Photo\\\" control only appends pre-set Unsplash sample images (helper text: \\\"Click to add sample images (up to 4)\\\"), so a seller cannot supply their own product photos. All other parts of the item worked: a listing created with title \\\"QA Upcycled Crate Shelf\\\", description, price 42.50, category Furniture, condition Good, location Brooklyn NY and upcycled=true was saved and its detail page displayed all of that (price rendered \\\"$42.5\\\").\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-2\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Listing editing is not implemented\", \"actual\": \"No edit affordance exists anywhere for an owned listing. My Listings offers only View, Mark Sold and Delete (no \\\"Edit\\\" string appears on the page at all), the product detail page for an owned listing offers only \\\"Manage Your Listings\\\", and the direct route /edit-listing/<id> renders the 404 \\\"Oops! Page not found\\\" page. Title, description, photos, price, category, condition, location and upcycled status therefore cannot be changed after creation.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-3\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"As Marcus: \\\"Mark Sold\\\" on prod-2 flipped its status observable to \\\"Sold\\\" and the button to \\\"Mark Available\\\" instantly; clicking again restored \\\"Active\\\". \\\"Mark Sold\\\" on prod-6 set it to Sold. Delete opened the \\\"Delete listing?\\\" confirmation dialog — Cancel left prod-2 in the list; confirming with Delete removed prod-2 from My Listings immediately, leaving only prod-6.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-4\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After Marcus marked prod-6 (Harry Potter Book Set) sold and deleted prod-2 (Denim Jacket), browse dropped from 10 to \\\"8 items available\\\" with neither id present. As buyer Sofia, searching \\\"harry potter\\\" and \\\"denim\\\" each returned \\\"0 items available\\\"/\\\"No items found\\\", and the Categories page counts fell to Books 0 items and Clothing 0 items — so neither listing is reachable to be added to a cart or messaged.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-5\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Registered Quinn Tester / quinn.tester@example.com / \\\"abc123456\\\" / Austin, TX: toast \\\"Account created successfully!\\\", redirected to /, header switched to signed-in (Sell + cart + user menu). A 5-character password was blocked first by minLength=6 validation (\\\"Please lengthen this text to 6 characters or more\\\").\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No maximum-price filter (price slider has a single min-only thumb); distance is not measured from the buyer's location\", \"actual\": \"The price filter renders only ONE thumb (aria-valuemin=0, aria-valuemax=500); moving it sets the LOWER bound only (label became \\\"$250 - $500\\\"), so a buyer cannot set a maximum price — the upper bound is permanently $500. Distance also ignores the signed-in buyer's location: as Quinn Tester (Austin, TX), setting the distance filter to 3 miles returned only the two Brooklyn, NY items and excluded all three Austin, TX items, and \\\"Sort: Distance\\\" ordered Brooklyn first and Austin second. Category, condition, upcycled-only and price-minimum filters do combine correctly (Furniture+New+Upcycled+min $250 → only the $320 Reclaimed Wood Bookshelf), and price sorting is correct ($35→$320).\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Title match \\\"DENIM\\\" → 1 item (Vintage Denim Jacket); location match \\\"portland\\\" → 3 items, all Portland, OR (prod-10, prod-3, prod-8); description-only match \\\"UPHOLSTERY\\\" → 1 item (Mid-Century Modern Armchair, whose description mentions upholstery). All matched despite case differences; clearing the box restored 10 items available.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"As Quinn Tester, added prod-8 ($125, James Wilson) — clicking Add to Cart twice kept the badge at 1, so the item is retained once. Added prod-9 ($35). Cart shows \\\"2 items\\\": \\\"Vintage Brass Floor Lamp / Portland, OR / $125\\\" and \\\"Kids Wooden Train Set / Austin, TX / $35\\\", each with its own product photo (img alt matches the title), and Total $160.00 = 125 + 35.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"As Quinn Tester on Marcus Chen's prod-2, \\\"Message Seller\\\" opened the dialog; with an empty textarea the Send button was disabled (enabled:false), and after typing \\\"Hi Marcus, is the denim jacket still available? ... - QA test\\\" the send succeeded with the visible confirmation toast \\\"Message sent to seller!\\\" and the dialog closed.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-21\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Category tile on the Categories page does not apply the category filter\", \"actual\": \"Clicking \\\"Home Decor 2 items\\\" on /categories navigated to /?category=home-decor but browse showed all 10 listings and the count read \\\"10 items available\\\"; every category checkbox in the filter panel remained unchecked, i.e. the ?category= query parameter is ignored. (By contrast, the category shortcut on the home page itself works: it produced \\\"2 items available\\\" with exactly the Macrame Wall Hanging and Brass Floor Lamp.)\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-22\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Sellers have no view of purchase requests; request confirmations are not backed by any recorded request\", \"actual\": \"Buyer sofia@example.com sent a message request on Marcus Chen's prod-2 containing \\\"QA-REQUEST-MARKER...\\\" (toast \\\"Message sent to seller!\\\"), and a cart request for two of Marcus's items reported \\\"Purchase requests sent to sellers!\\\". Signing in as marcus@example.com afterwards, no request is visible anywhere: /my-listings shows only the listing cards (no request/message/inquiry text, marker absent), the owned product detail page shows only \\\"Manage Your Listings\\\", and the user-menu \\\"My Profile\\\" link navigates to /profile which renders the 404 \\\"Oops! Page not found\\\" page. The cart flow also emptied the cart and reported success immediately with no per-item request record to verify.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-10\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Login with nobody-unregistered-9x@example.com rejected: \\\"Invalid credentials. Try: emma@example.com\\\", stayed on /login, header still shows Log in/Sign up, no session stored.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Registering \\\"emma@example.com\\\" and the case-only variant \\\"EMMA@Example.COM\\\" were both rejected with \\\"An account with this email already exists\\\"; stayed on /register, no session created, existing Emma Green account untouched.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Password is not verified; any password authenticates a registered account\", \"actual\": \"Signing in as emma@example.com with the arbitrary password \\\"definitely-the-wrong-password-zzz\\\" succeeded: redirected to / and header switched to the signed-in state (Sell link shown). The login page itself states \\\"Demo accounts ... (any password works)\\\", confirming passwords are never checked.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Viewing James Wilson's prod-8 as Quinn Tester shows only buyer actions (Add to Cart, Message Seller) and no Manage/Mark Sold/Delete anywhere. On an owned listing (Emma viewing her own prod-1787872385465) the buyer actions were replaced by a \\\"Manage Your Listings\\\" link, and /my-listings listed only that seller's own items with View/Mark Sold/Delete.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Empty submit blocked by native required validation on title/description/price (\\\"Please fill out this field.\\\"); missing category/condition blocked with \\\"Please fill in all required fields\\\"; all fields filled but no photo blocked with \\\"Please add at least one image\\\". No listing created in any case (stayed on /create-listing).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Price is input[type=number][min=0][step=0.01][required]. Submitting -10 was rejected (\\\"Value must be greater than or equal to 0.\\\") and no listing was created; non-numeric text cannot be entered into the number input at all.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-23\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Protected pages render a blank page instead of a sign-in prompt or redirect\", \"actual\": \"Gated actions on the product page behave correctly (unauthenticated \\\"Add to Cart\\\" redirects to /login; \\\"Message Seller\\\" shows \\\"Log in to message\\\"). But visiting the protected pages while signed out renders a completely empty page with no message and no redirect: /cart, /create-listing and /my-listings all return document.body.innerText.length === 0 and an accessibility snapshot containing only the notification regions. Access is blocked, but there is no clear sign-in prompt or redirect.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Duplicate-email submit showed the inline toast \\\"An account with this email already exists\\\" immediately without navigation, and the form stayed populated (name/email/password/location values retained) and editable for correction.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Typing \\\"DENIM\\\" character-by-character updated results and the count to \\\"1 items available\\\" with no submit button pressed and no Enter key; each subsequent query change (portland → 3, UPHOLSTERY → 1) and clearing (→ 10) updated the list and count immediately.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Each filter/sort change re-rendered instantly with no reload: Furniture → 3 items, +New → 2, +Upcycled → 2, price min $250 → 1, distance 3 mi → 2, sort price-low and distance reordered the grid; the count observable tracked every change. Turning the category/condition/upcycled filters back off and resetting the price slider restored \\\"10 items available\\\", the full unfiltered set.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-19\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicking Add to Cart showed the toast \\\"Added to cart!\\\" immediately and the header cart badge went 0→1→2 in place with no reload; the cart page then showed the matching line items, count \\\"2 items\\\" and total $160.00.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Detail pages present every required field consistently with the listing data. prod-8: photo gallery (prev/next), \\\"Vintage Brass Floor Lamp\\\", $125, Home Decor, Like New, \\\"Portland, OR (7 mi)\\\", seller James Wilson, \\\"Listed 2024-11-17\\\", description, and an \\\"Upcycled\\\" badge — matching its browse card ($125 / Portland, OR / Like New / Upcycled). prod-6: $95, Books, Good, San Francisco CA, Marcus Chen, Listed 2024-11-10, no Upcycled badge (correctly absent), and after being marked sold its detail shows the availability notice \\\"This item is no longer available\\\"; available listings instead show Add to Cart with no such notice. The listing I created also displayed back every submitted value including the Upcycled badge.\"}]}"
